{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick","id":1338431,"title":"Fame as Countermagick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-29T03:53:32-07:00","id":1338431,"title":"Fame as Countermagick","content":"Why don't world leaders get offed by Mages? Well, perhaps they do sometimes. But we can assume that within the WoD it isn't normal for a PM, President or Monarch's head to randomly explode, even though the Sphere system gives many ways to pull that off.<br /> <br /> An idea I had was that Fame acts as a very situational form of countermagick. The idea is that famous people (measured by the Fame background) are heavily embedded in the consensus of the reality zone. They're just as likely as anyone to have a random heart attack, but attempting to force a cardiac arrest with Life and Correspondence will be harder (they roll countermagick equal to their Fame rating). Metaphysically it's a matter of the consensus &quot;protecting&quot; an important figure of attention within it. This could apply to places and objects too.<br /> <br /> This protection is much more limited than the countermagick given by Primium and True Faith. It only effects attempts to directly change the target in a way that would defy the consensus. You can't mind-control a famously sensible and careful politician to go on a racist diatribe. Their Fame rating steps in... which is no guarantee of protection, but combined with decent Willpower and an effect that demands many successes it is unlikely to work. But if they're infamous for such rants, there's no such protection. Triggering a stroke in a politician who is publicly known to be extremely unhealthy means the protection isn't there, but making a relatively healthy (and this includes some extremely old) celebrity fall over dead from a heart attack is much harder. This would ultimately come down to ST caveat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-29-2019, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T09:55:17-07:00","id":1338471,"title":"","content":"The NWO would love this: use propaganda to slime up someone's reputation, then use mind control on the victim to compel him to act according to the propaganda. <br /> <br /> Admittedly, that would still be harder than just using mind control on the victim <i>without</i> first trashing his reputation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-29-2019, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T10:01:01-07:00","id":1338473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick?p=1338471#post1338471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The NWO would love this: use propaganda to slime up someone's reputation, them use mind control on the victim to compel him to act according to the propaganda.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, that would still be harder than just using mind control on the victim <i>without</i> first trashing his reputation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very NWO. Change the story, and then change the reality. I'm reminded of that Bond villain, the Murdoch stand-in: &quot;Tomorrow's News Today&quot;.<br /> <br /> And honestly I can imagine the NWO much preferring to invest effort in changing perceptions *before* they use psychodynamic conditioning. The NWO aren't shy about discussing the Enlightened Anthropic Principle, so I can easily see them performing character assassination prior to using Mind on someone to confirm the stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T10:09:15-07:00","id":1338475,"title":"","content":"That honestly seems fairly reasonable to me, and I'm surprised I've never seen someone suggest it over the decades I've been playing and following Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T12:00:54-07:00","id":1338494,"title":"","content":"I'd do the same thing for history events and people. Not sure if I'd rate history 1-5 or 1-10, but lets say you wanna go back in time to kill hitler with magick. Hitler was a pretty important figure so you'd probably have like, a counter magick rating of 5 for him.<br /> But towards the time of his death it would get lower and lower and I'd even give a bonus if you tried to kill hitler literally the same month/day he died, especially for figures who didn't have obvious deaths or clear deaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T21:22:44-07:00","id":1338563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick#post1338431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't world leaders get offed by Mages? Well, perhaps they do sometimes. But we can assume that within the WoD it isn't normal for a PM, President or Monarch's head to randomly explode, even though the Sphere system gives many ways to pull that off.<br /> <br /> &lt;...&gt;<br /> <br /> They're just as likely as anyone to have a random heart attack, but attempting to force a cardiac arrest with Life and Correspondence will be harder (they roll countermagick equal to their Fame rating)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmh. I love the concept of this overall, but realistically that'd not change much in regards to Mages being able to offing known authority figures or famous people.<br /> <br /> It's essentially &quot;<i>This effect needs about 3 more successes if the person has Fame 5(!)</i>&quot;. Which, if the mage is doing a ritual (and I hope they do - using a Ritual to off a person from afar is a big trope!) isn't that much of a deal.<br /> <br /> Now, if it's houseruled that countermagick applies to every single roll in a ritual even before the effect has been unleashed, instead of the end result of successes, then we're talking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T22:27:58-07:00","id":1338569,"title":"","content":"While the idea has merit, I seem to vaguely recall it being canon in WoD that the American president is protected by a powerful Umbrood, keeping supernaturals from exerting influence on them. I suspect such would also be true of other major nation states, whose spiritual embodiment is strong enough to protect its leader (at least from supernatural powers).<br /> <br /> I'm imagining some wily mage or werewolf trying to sneak into the White House on the Umbra side, only to be confronted by Uncle Sam. (<a href=\"http://drmcninja.com/archives/comic/28p29/\" target=\"_blank\">Or a figure with a bald eagle for a head</a>).<br /> <br /> Then again, I also like the idea that the Founding Fathers used Freemason rituals to ward the heck out of the White House. And then you have the Technocracy, which generally cares less about who is in the White House, and more about maintaining a stable balance of power. So whatever defenses the president has, the Union works in the background to shoo off what threats they can catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 09-30-2019, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T06:09:19-07:00","id":1338608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick?p=1338563#post1338563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if it's houseruled that countermagick applies to every single roll in a ritual even before the effect has been unleashed, instead of the end result of successes, then we're talking...</div> </div> </div> </div>Though I understand the logic here, if this was/is how countermagic were to work it would be WAY to effective. Especially against other supernaturals of which it is already somewhat overpowering depending on which rules you use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T07:17:44-07:00","id":1338622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick?p=1338608#post1338608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I understand the logic here, if this was/is how countermagic were to work it would be WAY to effective. Especially against other supernaturals of which it is already somewhat overpowering depending on which rules you use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it?. What Ambrosia suggests would only take place against powers that have extended activation rolls. I was under the impression supernatural powers with extended rolls were rare outside Mage (and those who do use them would still fare better than Mages because they often roll repeatedly with two dicepools against just Arete, unless we change that too)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-30-2019, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T14:27:59-07:00","id":1338693,"title":"","content":"I think Tuch is referring to the rather harsh (i.e. potent) countermagicks that nightfolk have against Mages, per vanilla M20 RAW. (Rules that i still don't really agree with in several parts, really...)<br /> <br /> Now, that said..remember that that countermagick houserule would also protect *your* mage better from getting instafried from afar, because that Nephandus that you are chasing? They can nuke your ass just as easily from the comfort of their ritual chamber per the normal rules...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-30-2019, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T04:57:10-07:00","id":1338766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick?p=1338693#post1338693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Tuch is referring to the rather harsh (i.e. potent) countermagicks that nightfolk have against Mages, per vanilla M20 RAW. (Rules that i still don't really agree with in several parts, really...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's true.<br /> <br /> I forgot those rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T12:47:55-07:00","id":1338857,"title":"","content":"This is a great idea. It would also make the Fame Background more worthwhile to players, since at the moment it seems to mostly just paint a target on your back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T15:10:07-07:00","id":1338875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick?p=1338857#post1338857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great idea. It would also make the Fame Background more worthwhile to players, since at the moment it seems to mostly just paint a target on your back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah in the WoD setting a high profile seems to be a very &quot;mixed&quot; blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T15:14:38-07:00","id":1338876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick?p=1338563#post1338563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmh. I love the concept of this overall, but realistically that'd not change much in regards to Mages being able to offing known authority figures or famous people.<br /> <br /> It's essentially &quot;<i>This effect needs about 3 more successes if the person has Fame 5(!)</i>&quot;. Which, if the mage is doing a ritual (and I hope they do - using a Ritual to off a person from afar is a big trope!) isn't that much of a deal.<br /> <br /> Now, if it's houseruled that countermagick applies to every single roll in a ritual even before the effect has been unleashed, instead of the end result of successes, then we're talking...</div> </div> </div> </div>- yes you're right, against powerful mages this protection would be very minor indeed<br /> <br /> - it applying to each roll would be a good idea since the negative effect on a quick spell is proportional to the negative effect on a ritual<br /> <br /> - this also means that the protection makes it harder to pull off these effects across a wide range of power levels, without making it truly &quot;impossible&quot; for anyone (weaker mages can rope in cult or allies to succeed, increasing their dice and automatic successes)<br /> <br /> - would there be any serious consequences to ALL countermagick working this way? I feel like Primium is already a very good investment. If this would be &quot;OP&quot; in other contexts when I could imagine limiting it to the Fame background, and only applying it to the situations described above with some ST caveat to figure out the fine detail","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T10:07:16-07:00","id":1339210,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the countermagick be applied to the first roll and only the first roll? So say, you roll 5 dice, get 4 successes, countermagick counters that. Ritual fails. Start over.<br /> <br /> That's how I thought it worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T11:15:51-07:00","id":1339216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1338431-fame-as-countermagick?p=1339210#post1339210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the countermagick be applied to the first roll and only the first roll?<br /> <br /> So say, you roll 5 dice, get 4 successes, countermagick counters that. Ritual fails. Start over.<br /> <br /> That's how I thought it worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, maybe it's not 100% clear in Revised, but I don't think so: Rituals and Extended Rolls are allocated under Step 3, Countermagic was allocated under Step 4 (p.152). Step 4 assumes you know enough to determine Damage, Duration and all that. In a Ritual you would need to wait until the last roll to know that with precision.<br /> <br /> In 2 edition it was a bit more clear that it was to be used after the effect had been cast (described as a sort of &quot;soak roll&quot;, and also under Step 4)<br /> <br /> If that wasn't the case, there's still the point that Rituals can keep going after a failure. At a +1 diff per each failure, but they don't start over (successes aren't lost).<br /> <br /> Now, one could say that functionally starting at 0 successes it's the same thing as starting over. Fair enough, but there's some related mechanics that may need to be adressed in that case. Like, say, the ST can decide that a certain ritual has a lapse of 1 hour between Arete rolls: If you fail and start over, you can start right away or you have to wait the time between rolls as if the ritual had keep going?. I can see arguments for either case<br /> <br /> Also, the purpose of Countermagick it's often not to cancel ALL the successes of the enemy, but cancelling enough (Counter difficulty it's often quite high. 8 in Revised). Canceling just two or tree Successes on a 4 success roll could be enough to down the Potency of the Effect to the point it does nothing (Effects tend to need more than 1 success). Nedless to say, this wouldn't be useful for a Ritual because to keep going after you got 1 success doesn't do anything against the Ritual.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> That being said, your way of ruling this does make Countermagic more relevant to rituals. Which ain't bad in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-03-2019, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}